(1679786, 23820, 29168, '<td valign="top">It seems to me many people can''t break away from "photograph" to see "art". I wonder -- if an "artist" used cut up photos to form an interesting collage if fellow artists would cry "film! yuck!" &lt;sigh&gt;<br/> <br/>I think this is a really good artistic effort. It oozes "fluid" to me -- especially in the context of the title. The blur of adds to "fluid" rather than detracts IMO. I would have scored it an 8 or 9 at least.<br/> <br/>I wont even comment on the "hairy arms / masculine" thing. &lt;deep sigh&gt; I find such comments quite upsetting.</td>', 'It seems to me many people can''t break away from "photograph" to see "art". I wonder -- if an "artist" used cut up photos to form an interesting collage if fellow artists would cry "film! yuck!" <sigh> I think this is a really good artistic effort. It oozes "fluid" to me -- especially in the context of the title. The blur of adds to "fluid" rather than detracts IMO. I would have scored it an 8 or 9 at least. I wont even comment on the "hairy arms / masculine" thing. <deep sigh> I find such comments quite upsetting.', '2005-09-06 19:20:10.000000', NULL, 0),
